    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// A 7/8 melody over a 4/4 drum (docs/plan/prompts/75)." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Polymeter, in the shape that costs something: the bars are different" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// *lengths*, so the barlines genuinely diverge and only meet again after" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// seven whole notes — eight bars of 7/8 against seven of 4/4. A Balkan" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// ensemble plays this without remarking on it, which is the point: it is" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// ordinary music, and a program that cannot write it cannot write the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// repertoire." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// A part's meter is written in the part, like its clef, and it is in force" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// for the whole part. `Meter` inherits by `Override`, so the kaval does not" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// rejoin the piece's 4/4 at any point — a 7/8 lane that quietly resumed" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// counting in 4 would be a different piece." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// What the exports make of it is worth reading. `MusicXML` has a `<measure>`" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// list per part, so it says this exactly. `LilyPond` says it once Timing is" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// moved from Score to Staff, which the export does. MEI numbers measures for" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// the *score*, so it can state each staff's meter but not give each its own" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// barlines — and the exporter says so rather than letting it be discovered." },
